=== interpretation, added after the run ===

HARNESS VALIDATION: each member reproduces its own recorded full_valid_wp to
within 6e-5 (v028: 0.686449 vs 0.686510) and 2e-4 (v029: 0.684498 vs 0.684683),
which is float32 drift over 20,000 recurrent steps. So the -0.000174 below is a
real measurement and not a pipeline artifact.

RESULT: NULL. The 2-member mean lands 0.000174 BELOW v028 alone, well inside the
+/-0.000317 noise floor. dozken measured +0.0056 at P(>0)=1.000 for a loss-diverse
pair, so this is a refutation rather than an uninformative null.

WHY, and it is not mysterious. Our two members are not actually diverse.
Their scores differ by 0.00195; his differ by 0.0041. More decisively, v029
differs from v028 only by gamma=2.0 tail-weighting on the DISTILL term, and that
was already measured as a dead null in its own right (+0.000002, idea 5). A knob
that provably does nothing cannot manufacture ensemble diversity. We applied his
mechanism -- members trained with different losses -- to two members whose losses
were, in effect, the same.

LESSON: a loss-diverse ensemble requires members whose individual optimisation
genuinely diverges. It is not enough to vary a hyper-parameter; the variation has
to show up in the member scores.
